# Fibonacci Series

Given an integer `N`, find the Nth number in the Fibonacci Series.

The Fibonacci Series is:

0 1 1 2 3 5 8 13 ...

Each number is the sum of the previous two numbers.

## Examples

N = 1 → 0

N = 2 → 1

N = 7 → 8

## Approach

Use recursion.

Base cases:

fib(1) = 0
fib(2) = 1

For N > 2:

fib(N) = fib(N-1) + fib(N-2)

## Complexity

Time: O(2^N)
Space: O(N)

## Constraints

- 1 <= N <= 100
